$MDESC::Type = "Football";
$MDESC::Text = "<s3><f1>Mission Type: <f0> Football" @
         "\n<f1>Stadium: <f0> PikaDrop Stadium" @
         "\n<f1>Weather: <f0> Clear" @
         "\n<f1>Time of Day: <f0> Night" @ 
         "\n<f1># of Teams: <f0> 2" @
         "\n\n<f1>Briefing:<f0> Uhm...ok this mapper is on crack.  Pikaaaaaaaaaaaaaa!"@
	 "\n\nOkay, so maybe you`re wondering why name it PikaDrop Stadium.  Well, let us dissect the word choice.  'Pika', an obvious reference to the lovable yellow creature made popular by the imported japanese anime (yes, its anime like it or not) series Pokémon.  'Drop', well thats what you do while playing the map.  'PikaDrop' though has other roots, namely 'PikaJumping' in Unreal Tournament`s popular mod, Strike Force (soon to be coming to the Tribes 2 gaming engine, check it out at http://www.strikeforceceneter.com/).  'PikaJumping' is the trademark suicide death born into existance by the The Great Hamster Clan, tag name (TGHC).  'PikaJumping' unfortunately causes death, for technical reasons not allowing you to score, and you are required to initiate the jump.  'PikaDropping' however, is simply the act of falling - perhaps to your death, though not in this case - making it a much more apt description of what takes place.  Anyhow, enjoy the map."@
         "\n\n<f1>Map by:<f0> Lackey No. 2";

